def search_range(arr, target):
    def find_bound(find_first):
        lo, hi = 0, len(arr) - 1
        result = -1
        while lo <= hi:
            mid = lo + (hi - lo) // 2
            if arr[mid] == target:
                result = mid
                if find_first:
                    hi = mid - 1     # keep searching left for an earlier match
                else:
                    lo = mid + 1     # keep searching right for a later match
            elif arr[mid] < target:
                lo = mid + 1
            else:
                hi = mid - 1
        return result

    return [find_bound(True), find_bound(False)]
```

One small helper, parameterized by direction, covers both first and last occurrence — the only difference between the two calls is which side keeps narrowing after a match is found.

